error[E0906]: `type_info` can't describe `Type`, which exists only while compiling
  --> tests/ui/type_info_errors.wid:14:13
   |
14 |   type_info(t).size
   |             ^ this `Type` value exists only while compiling
   = note: `type_info` returns a table the program keeps while it runs
help: to describe the type it holds, read it while compiling with `t.name`, `t.size`, `t.align` and `t.fields`, or pass the type itself, like `type_info(Ball)`
   = see `wid explain E0906`

error[E0905]: this `^TypeInfo` can't be used at run time: it holds a pointer into compile-time memory
  --> tests/ui/type_info_errors.wid:17:8
   |
17 | LEAK = comptime type_info(Ball)
   |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ computed while compiling
   = note: values made at compile time are copied into the program; memory the compiler used is not
help: a `type_info` table built while compiling stays in the compiler: call `type_info` in code that runs, or keep only what you need, like `comptime type_info(T).size`
   = see `wid explain E0905`

